; Sheep — generated by scripts/asset_pipeline.py run 20260830-sheep-5652
; Source: source-content/assets/Farm Animals by @Quaternius/Blends/Sheep.blend
; Format: blend (no gltf in pack; blend carries 2 of the 2 required clips vs fbx's 1)
; Every value below was ruled by the human at this run's checkpoint.
;
; TIERS — RE-SPEC 2026-09-04 (habitat tiers).
;
; PROPOSAL, NOT A DECISION. Every divisor and cap below is this design's own first-pass
; proposal awaiting human sign-off, per the project rule that all tuning values are the
; human's. Source: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-habitat-tiers-design.md § 9.
;
; TWO TIERS: "base" (`open_grass/4` `people/3` — a sheep follows the villagers who keep it,
; not a building) and "flock" (the same needs plus `mill`, arriving in groups of 4) — wool
; needs somewhere to be milled, so a windmill nearby is what grows a pair into a flock.
;
; INTERPRETATION FLAG: the spec table writes the flock tier's added need as bare `mill`,
; with no `/divisor` and no explicit `*`. Read here as GATE_ONLY (present-or-not, matching
; the windmill's role as a landmark rather than a scaling resource) — the human should
; confirm this reading or supply a divisor.
;
; The legacy flat fields (habitat_needs / tiles_per_individual / max_individuals) are LEFT
; IN PLACE and are now inert: `effective_tiers()` prefers `tiers` when non-empty. They are
; retained so a rollback is a one-line edit rather than a re-authoring.
